 A three-level hierarchical traversal method that separates traversal into draining the current I1 DDA, stepping the I2 DDA, and advancing to the next root entry. It differs from MultiDDA by managing three distinct node types (I2, I1, leaf) rather than two levels of DDA loops.
 
+### Rasterized Brick AABB Depth Buffer
+A hybrid rendering technique where camera-facing brick faces are rasterized into a depth buffer [S2, unofficial]. Ray tracing uses this depth buffer to determine the ray origin for DDA, allowing it to skip empty space much faster [S2, unofficial]. Quads are regenerated every frame to support dynamic voxel grids [S2, unofficial]. Tighter fitting (4x4x4) improves performance when close to the model surface; looser (8x8x8) is better when viewing from afar [S2, unofficial]. Performance uplift: sponza-1024-1 FPS +28.99%, sponza-1024-2 FPS +36.64% [S2, unofficial].
